this is my third time as a presenter at  the student Oscars in the last 25 years  and I just want to say I really think  this is a terrific event and for those I  haven't bored enough already the first  time I did this I gave out the animation  one to a young kid named John Lasseter  so I wish you all the same success our  bronze medal winner was made at a school  that had a winning documentary in our  Awards last year as well made at  American University in Washington DC  filmmaker Lauren DeAngelis chronicles  the complications and challenges  inherent and dealing with parrots both  in the wild and as pets please welcome  the director of a place to land Lauren  DeAngelis Lauren making this film has  been without a doubt one of the most  incredible and rewarding experiences of  my life and being here today and meeting  so many talented filmmakers this week  has been another incredible experience  and one that I never expected what  actually happened to me something else I  never expected occurred when I was 10  years old and my mother gave in and  bought my sister and I a pet parrot this  is the same woman who refused to let us  keep a goldfish we wanted a school  carnival but regardless we came home  with the parrot we named it precious and  precious is now 18 years old and without  her in my life I never would have  realized the difficulties that captive  parrots face and I might not be standing  here today so first I'd like to thank my  mother for her lapse in judgment that  day and for always believing in me since  then I'd also like to thank my father  for his support and advice over the  years and for putting up with a parrot  flying around the house sometimes at his  head next I'd like to thank my  professors at American University for  giving me the confidence and the  knowledge to produce a film from start  to finish I'd like to thank the members  of the Academy for hosting us here this  week for seeing my film and believing in  it and giving me this incredible  opportunity I'd like to thank my friends  and family who are here in the audience  today supporting me  and I'd like to thank the other half of  my two-person crew Joe Bohannon as my  talented cinematographer and sound  technician he literally scaled mountains  to get some of the shots i wanted to  flying birds he is not only a dedicated  colleague but a true friend as well and  finally I'd like to thank the hard  working people and rescue groups who  helped parrots every single day parrots  may be able to imitate our words but  they have no real voice to tell us what  they need or how they want us to treat  them so I truly hope that this award  really helps give greater get  recognition to their plate thank you  you
 

